    "result_text": "There's a single test class in the suite, and it passes (BUILD SUCCESS). \n\nDone. Summary of the change:\n\n**Spec:** return `telephoneDisplay` = the stored E.164 telephone formatted for humans (`+61412345678` \u2192 `+61 412 345 678`), keeping `telephone` as raw E.164.\n\n**Implementation** \u2014 kept structural impact low by adding a small cohesive unit rather than growing any existing class:\n\n1. **New `TelephoneDisplay` helper** (`rest/function/owner/TelephoneDisplay.java`) \u2014 one public static `of(String e164)`. It splits the country code using the same codes `BuildOwner` recognises (`+61`, `+1`), then groups the national digits in threes. All the logic lives here, in a brand-new class with zero surrounding complexity.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 one added `@Mapping` line delegating to the helper via a MapStruct expression, matching the existing pattern for `ageBand`, `locality`, etc. The `toOwnerDto` method's body (empty, generated) is untouched.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `telephoneDisplay` property to the `Owner` schema so the generated DTO gets the field/setter.\n\nThe acceptance test (`telephone` `\"+61412345678\"`, `telephoneDisplay` `\"+61 412 345 678\"`) and the full build pass.",
